  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEC funded emergency assistance to Ukrainian refugees arriving in Romania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partner: JRS Romania (via JRS Europe)

Funding source: DEC appeal

Context: This has been a stabilisation of the numbers of Ukrainians seeking refuge in Romania but by no means a cessation of the flow. There is still a need to identify and support those that are not covered by the European Union&#x2019;s Temporary Protection Mechanism (TPM) or the Romanian Government&#x2019;s Emergency Ordinance, and to support those who are able to qualify in accessing the support available.

Key activities: providing shelter, living allowance, communications and legal advice to Ukrainians arriving in Romania.

Activity split:
10%: Food, nutrition &amp; livelihoods in emergencies
10%: Health in emergencies
10%: Non-food items in emergencies
20%: Protection in emergencies
50%: Shelter in emergencies</narrative>
  </description>
